{
  "requirement": "When `habeas author` assesses a subject with existing evidence, that evidence\nMUST only determine whether the subject needs assessment. Its inputs,\ndetermination, and rationale MUST NOT contribute to the mandatory input set\ndefined by {cite}`requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs` or otherwise be\nsupplied to the model. A new assessment's evidence MUST record only the inputs\nsupplied to it, so sources that an earlier assessment read but that no longer\nexist or are no longer relevant cannot block or shape reassessment.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is implemented and tested.** The two parts of the requirement are existing evidence deciding only whether to reassess, and a new record containing only the inputs actually supplied.\n\n**Implementation**\n\n- **Existing evidence decides only whether to reassess.**\n  - `select_subjects` in `src/authoring/batch.rs` reads an existing record only through `LoadedDetailEvidence::state()`. A subject is skipped only when the state is Valid, Fixme or DeterminationFalse; otherwise it is queued.\n  - `author_all_with_options` carries the `{impl}` marker for this requirement.\n  - No code in `src/authoring` passes the existing record's inputs, determination or rationale to the model. `configured_record` and `converse` do not read it.\n  - The confirmation follow-ups build fresh sources through `followup_sources`, not from the earlier record.\n- **Mandatory input set (`AssessmentSources::prepare`, `src/authoring/inputs.rs`).**\n  - The set is built only from the subject, its `{cite}` targets, the `{impl}`/`{test}` references and anchors, term dependencies, and built-ins.\n  - The code comment states \"Existing evidence only decides whether to reassess; its inputs are not carried forward\".\n  - Generated `evidence/` output (including symlink aliases) is omitted by default through `omit_generated_evidence`, `generated_evidence_path` and `generated_evidence_selector`. An explicit allow lifts the omission, and a disallow still aborts through `check_disallow` and `read_denial`. This matches the `mandatory_inputs` requirement it cites.\n- **New evidence records only supplied inputs.**\n  - `AssessmentSources.recorded` starts empty.\n  - `converse` calls `record_inputs` only after a successful provider response, and only with the inputs in `pending` (the mandatory set plus tool deliveries).\n  - `record()` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` writes `sources.recorded_inputs()`, so stale or removed sources from an earlier record cannot appear in it.\n  - `write_record` replaces the file atomically.\n- **Unresolvable earlier inputs cannot block reassessment.** `prepare` never parses or resolves the old record's inputs, so missing files, removed items and removed requirements in an old record have no effect.\n- **Marking.** The `{impl}` markers on `omit_generated_evidence`, `author_all_with_options`, `prepare`, `generated_evidence_path`, `generated_evidence_selector`, `source_input` and `converse` cover the relevant code. I found no unmarked code implementing a part of this requirement, and no behaviour that goes beyond it.\n\n**Tests (`src/authoring/inputs.rs`)**\n\n- `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` writes an old record with a false determination, the rationale \"old secret judgment\" and a `notes.txt` input. It asserts that `notes.txt` and the old rationale are absent from the mandatory inputs, and that `recorded_inputs()` is empty. It also checks the positive contributions (`{impl}`/`{test}` items, `{cite}`d requirements, the two term definitions).\n- `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` writes an old record naming a missing file, a removed Rust item and a removed requirement. `prepare` still succeeds and yields exactly the subject input, while an unknown subject still errors.\n- `earlier_evidence_inputs_and_judgments_are_not_carried_forward` covers an old record that includes an `evidence/…` input pointing at itself. It checks the supplied inputs contain no `notes.txt`, no `evidence/` and no old rationale, and that the old file is unchanged.\n- The `evidence/` omission and its allow/disallow overrides are exercised by the related access tests (`explicit_allow_overrides_defaults_but_disallow_wins_for_alias_targets`, `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation`).\n\n**Residual gap (not blocking).** There is no end-to-end test that a batch run on an invalid stale record writes a new record containing only the delivered inputs. The pieces are individually tested: `prepare` carries nothing forward, `record_inputs` records only what was delivered (`reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms`), and `record` writes only those. I consider this adequate.",
  "references": "50148c9cfa29314fa2a17847f5b31dd0d0dbff0707c70e2e20cb993a124bd5c8",
